## Quality Checklist

Before completing any documentation:
- [ ] Code examples verified against source code or reference apps
- [ ] Version numbers documented with dates
- [ ] Format matches templates (see research-writing-guide rule)
- [ ] No placeholder text remaining
- [ ] Pitfalls section has real gotchas (not generic)
- [ ] TypeScript signatures extracted from actual `.d.ts` files
- [ ] Callback/event signatures include full parameter types

## Documentation Standards

**TypeScript Types**: Always check `.d.ts` files. Don't guess signatures.

**Active Decision Trees**: Frame as directives:
- Bad: "Need local AI inference? Use QVAC SDK."
- Good: "If the user mentions AI/LLM, ASK: 'Do you need local inference (QVAC) or cloud API?'"

**Model/Variant Docs**: Document all options with tradeoff tables.

## Available Research Workflows

These rules activate based on file context or can be referenced:
- **research-writing-guide** — Templates for module and recipe docs
- **research-verify** — Audit agent pack content for quality and completeness
- **research-test-agent-pack** — Verify generated agent pack configs
- **research-improve-from-feedback** — Fix docs based on user error reports
- **research-scan-community** — Scan community for new patterns
- **research-feedback-fixer** — Triage app-build feedback into doc fixes
